{
  "version": "1.0",
  "id": "coord-machine-maintenance",
  "name": "Coord machine maintenance (admin)",
  "description": "One machine, one restart verdict, two levers (/admin/coord/machine-maintenance), plan 2026-09-28-machine-maintenance-pause-ci-and-drain-in-one-place Phase 7 — it replaced the Runner Drain page, and this spec replaces that page's spec. ci-bot is a superuser so the page renders its real content. The page reads its machine from `?machine=` (run-spec-ci.ts seeds the sentinel device below) and makes these reads: GET /api/v1/operations/fleet/machines (the picker and the machine's window — none open here, so no per-window readiness read is made), GET /fleet/drain (the drain badge), GET /fleet/ci-runners (the CI registrations shown while nothing is paused), GET /fleet/resource-samples?device_id=&history=false (the runner's readiness verdict) and GET /sessions/fleet?device_id= (the session census); the audit panel reads GET /coord/audit/recent. metadata.routeStubs fulfills all of them so the populated states render deterministically: a machine with no declared CI host and no open window, one fresh unsafe readiness sample whose wind_down_sessions name two sessions matched to two census rows. AUTHORED FROM SOURCE, NOT DERIVED, like the coord-runners spec it replaces: no dev stack or authed UI Bridge snapshot was available in the authoring session, so every criterion below is an authored data-testid read off the page and verified by page.specSelectors.test.tsx against a jsdom render, not a live capture. Re-derive from a live authed snapshot when one is available (console style guide §6.3). Read-only; structural only.",
